msgid "A recently verified appliance database backup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:13
msgid ""
"A filesystem-level backup of ``/var/opt/morpheus/morpheus-ui``, including"
" ownership and permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:14
msgid ""
"Protected copies of ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb``, ``/etc/morpheus"
"/morpheus-secrets.json``, certificates, and the deployment record "
"(appliance version, hostname, IP, DNS, gateway, and storage mappings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:16
msgid ""
"Protect the secrets file as credential material. Test recovery on the "
"same appliance version and document the recovery point and recovery time "
"achieved by the test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:18
#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:49
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:18
msgid ""
"The destination |morpheus| appliance must be running the same version as "
"that which the backup was taken from."
msgstr ""
"The destination |morpheus| appliance debe ser running the same version as"
" that which the backup was taken from."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:21
msgid "Create A Backup Job"
msgstr "Create A Backup Job"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:23
msgid ""
"A Backup Job in |morpheus| holds the schedule timing and retention count "
"for automated backups. If you already have a Job configured, you can move"
" on to the next section. By default, |morpheus| includes two execution "
"schedules: Daily at Midnight and Weekly on Sunday at Midnight. If "
"currently-existing options do not make sense for your backup needs, "
"create a new execution schedule:"
msgstr ""
"A Backup Job in |morpheus| holds the schedule timing y retention count "
"for automated backups. If you already have a Job configured, you can move"
" on to the next section. Por defecto, |morpheus| includes two execution "
"schedules: Daily at Midnight y Weekly on Sunday at Midnight. If "
"actualmente-existing options do no make sense for your backup needs, "
"create un nuevo execution schedule:"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:25
msgid "Navigate to :menuselection:`Library --> Automation`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:26
msgid "Click on the \"Execute Scheduling\" tab"
msgstr "Click on the \\\"Execute Scheduling\\\" tab"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:27
#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:34
#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:45
msgid "Click :guilabel:`+ ADD`"
msgstr "Click :guilabel:`+ ADD`"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:28
msgid "Enter schedule timing using ``cron`` notation"
msgstr "Enter schedule timing using ``cron`` notation"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:29
#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:36
#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:58
msgid "Click :guilabel:`SAVE`"
msgstr "Click :guilabel:`SAVE`"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:31
msgid ""
"With the execution schedule created, we can move on to creating the "
"Backup Job itself. A Backup Job includes both the backup retention count "
"and an execution schedule (which we just created)."
msgstr ""
"With the execution schedule created, we can move on to creating the "
"Backup Job itself. A Backup Job includes both the backup retention count "
"y an execution schedule (which we just created)."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:33
msgid "Navigate to Backups > Jobs"
msgstr "Navigate to Backups > Jobs"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:35
msgid "Name the Job, then configure the retention count and the schedule"
msgstr "Name the Job, then configure the retention count y the schedule"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:39
msgid "Integrate a Bucket or File Share"
msgstr "Integrate a Bucket o File Share"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:41
msgid ""
"When configuring a |morpheus| appliance backup, a storage location is "
"selected. If you already have the destination bucket or file share "
"integrated with |morpheus|, skip to the next section."
msgstr ""
"When configuring a |morpheus| appliance backup, a storage location is "
"selected. If you already have the destination bucket o file share "
"integrated con |morpheus|, skip to the next section."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:43
msgid "Navigate to Infrastructure > Storage"
msgstr "Navigate to Infrastructure > Storage"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:44
msgid ""
"Click on the Buckets or File Shares tab depending on your chosen storage "
"type"
msgstr ""
"Click en la Buckets o File Shares tab dependiendo de your chosen storage "
"type"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:46
msgid "Select the appropriate bucket or file share type"
msgstr "Select the apropiado bucket o file share type"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:47
msgid "Complete the required fields and click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"
msgstr "Complete the obligatorio fields y click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:49
msgid ""
"Additional guidance on integrating each of the supported bucket and file "
"share types can be found elsewhere in |morpheus| documentation."
msgstr ""
"Additional guidance on integrating each of the soportado bucket y file "
"share types puede ser found elsewhere in |morpheus| documentation."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:52
msgid "Configuring |morpheus| Appliance Backup"
msgstr "Configuring |morpheus| Appliance Backup"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:54
msgid ""
"With the groundwork laid in the previous sections, we're ready to enable "
"and configure |morpheus| appliance backup."
msgstr ""
"With the groundwork laid in the anterior sections, we're ready habilitar "
"y configure |morpheus| appliance backup."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:56
msgid "Navigate to |AdmSetBac|"
msgstr "Navigate to |AdmSetBac|"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:57
msgid "Slide the switch labeled \"Backup Appliance\""
msgstr "Slide the switch labeled \\\"Backup Appliance\\\""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:60
msgid ""
"On saving this change, a text link labeled \"Backup\" will be activated "
"which will take you directly to the automatically-generated appliance "
"backup job. Click this link to continue."
msgstr ""
"On saving this change, a text link labeled \\\"Backup\\\" será activated "
"which will take you directly to the automatically-generated appliance "
"backup job. Click this link to continue."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:62
msgid "Click :guilabel:`EDIT`"
msgstr "Click :guilabel:`EDIT`"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:63
msgid "Enter a name for the appliance backup job"
msgstr "Enter a name for el appliance backup job"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:64
msgid "Select an integrated storage bucket or file share"
msgstr "Select an integrated storage bucket o file share"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:65
msgid ""
"Choose a pre-created backup job. If you do not have an existing backup "
"job that fits, a retention count and schedule can be manually created in "
"this modal. If you manually configure retention counts and schedules in "
"addition to associating a Job, the Job values will override any manual "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"Choose a pre-created backup job. If you do not have an existing backup "
"job that fits, a retention count y schedule puede ser manually created in"
" this modal. If you manually configure retention counts y schedules "
"además de associating a Job, the Job values will override any manual "
"settings."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:66
msgid "Click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"
msgstr "Click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:68
msgid ""
"At this point, your appliance will be automatically backed up on the "
"schedule you chose and stored in the selected location. An appliance "
"backup will store backup copies of the appliance MySQL database. Should "
"you need to restore or migrate your database from backup, follow the "
"steps in the next section of this guide."
msgstr ""
"At this point, your appliance será automatically backed up on the "
"schedule you chose y stored in the selected location. An appliance backup"
" will store backup copies of el appliance MySQL database. Should you "
"necesitan restore o migrate your database desde backup, follow the steps "
"in the next section of this guide."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:71
msgid "Restoring an Appliance from Backup"
msgstr "Restoring an Appliance desde Backup"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:76
msgid "VME Manager host-failure decision tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:78
msgid ""
"First isolate the failed HVM host so that it cannot run another copy of "
"the Manager VM. Starting two copies with the same identity or disks can "
"corrupt data and disrupt integrations. Then select the recovery path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:80
msgid ""
"**The Manager VM and all of its disks are intact on storage accessible to"
" another healthy host:** use the supported HVM VM registration, "
"migration, or recovery workflow for the applicable cluster layout. This "
"relocates the complete VM; it is not an appliance database restore. "
"Preserve the VM identity, MAC addresses, and storage attachments. Start "
"only one copy and validate it using the checklist below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:81
msgid ""
"**The VM is unavailable, but the complete recovery set survives:** deploy"
" a replacement Manager at the **same version as the backup**, preserve or"
" deliberately update its DNS/IP identity, and contact HPE Support for the"
" topology-specific database and appliance-file restore sequence. Do not "
"attach the old and replacement Manager to production simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:82
msgid ""
"**Only a database backup survives:** stop. A database backup does not "
"contain all files, configuration, secrets, certificates, or uploaded "
"assets needed to reproduce the appliance. Contact HPE Support to "
"determine what can be recovered and which integrations and credentials "
"must be rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:83
msgid ""
"**No viable VM or recovery set survives:** deploy a new Manager and re-"
"onboard resources under an HPE Support recovery plan. Do not copy "
"database tables, edit appliance identity directly, or reuse unknown disks"
" in an attempt to reconstruct the failed appliance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:85
msgid ""
"Before any recovery, record the failed host and storage state, fence or "
"power off the original host, protect surviving disks from writes, and "
"take snapshots or storage-level copies where supported. Stop and contact "
"HPE Support if host isolation is uncertain, a disk is inconsistent, the "
"replacement version differs, the database topology is unknown, or "
"DNS/certificate/identity changes are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:87
msgid ""
"After starting the recovered Manager, verify the appliance URL and "
"certificate, administrator login, service health, database connectivity, "
"UI assets and uploaded images, HVM cluster/host connectivity, inventory "
"refresh, console access, integrations, automation credentials, and the "
"next appliance backup. Do not discard the failed VM or recovery artifacts"
" until this validation and an agreed rollback period are complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:89
msgid ""
"Begin by ensuring the Morpheus UI service is stopped on all of the "
"application servers:"
msgstr ""
"Begin by ensuring the Morpheus UI service is stopped on all of the "
"application servers:"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:91
msgid "[root@app-server-new ~] morpheus-ctl stop morpheus-ui"
msgstr "[root@app-server-new ~] morpheus-ctl stop morpheus-ui"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:95
msgid ""
"For an embedded database using the default generated credentials, "
"retrieve the exact MySQL application-user key without printing unrelated "
"secrets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:97
msgid ""
"[root@app-server-old ~] jq -r '.mysql.morpheus_password' /etc/morpheus"
"/morpheus-secrets.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:101
msgid ""
"For an external database or a customized database name, host, user, or "
"password, use the effective ``mysql`` configuration in "
"``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` instead. Values in ``morpheus-"
"secrets.json`` describe generated embedded-service secrets and must not "
"be assumed to describe an external service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:103
msgid ""
"Copy the SQL database backup from the backup bucket or file share to a "
"secured location on an appliance node. The previously documented direct "
"``mysql`` restore command is not a supported general restore procedure: "
"appliance dumps can contain database-level statements, and the correct "
"connection target, privileges, schema name, topology sequence, and "
"validation depend on the deployment. Contact HPE Support for the restore "
"command and recovery plan for the source and target appliance versions "
"and database topology. Do not start the UI until Support's restore "
"validation is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:105
msgid ""
"When the validated restore is complete, start the UI on each application "
"server as directed by the recovery plan:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/backup_restore.rst:107
msgid "[root@app-server-new ~] morpheus-ctl start morpheus-ui"
msgstr "[root@app-server-new ~] morpheus-ctl start morpheus-ui"

